### 3. Best Practices for Firebase Security

#### Firestore Security Rules
Rules must allow the initial profile creation while using custom claims to protect subsequent updates.

```javascript
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    match /users/{userId} {
      // Allow the user to read their own profile
      allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;

      // Allow the initial document creation during signup
      allow create: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;

      // Require the custom claim for updates to ensure the user 
      // has been processed by the backend
      allow update: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId 
                   && request.auth.token.signup_complete == true;
    }
  }
}
```

